name: hermesp2p
audience: public
description: >
  Decentralized ephemeral peer-to-peer messaging. No servers, no
  persistence. Ed25519 signing with NaCl encryption. Messages exist
  only in transit and in recipient memory. Deployed at hp2p.net.

domains:
  - p2p-networking
  - privacy
  - cryptography
  - ephemeral-messaging
  - decentralization

voice:
  tone: minimal, privacy-absolute
  principles:
    - No message persistence — ephemeral by architecture, not policy
    - Ed25519 identity is the only durable state
    - Peer discovery via signaling, not central registry
    - Padding defeats traffic analysis
  anti-patterns:
    - Storing messages on any server
    - Centralized peer registry
    - Unpadded messages that leak content length

standards:
  code_review:
    - NaCl for all encryption operations
    - Ed25519 for all signing
    - No server-side message storage under any condition
  documentation:
    - Protocol documented with wire format

connects_to:
  - signet
  - blinddb
  - tessera
  - agent-safe

work_policy:
  require_active_tag: false
  linear:
    enabled: false
    require_issue: false
  git:
    block_commit_without_tag: false
    block_commit_without_linear: false
    block_push_without_tag: false
    block_push_without_linear: false
